  "facts": [
    "Opened June 30, 1934, the Sumner Tunnel originally carried two‑way traffic until 1961, when the Callahan Tunnel opened and the Sumner was converted to one‑way flow under Boston Harbor.",
    "Named after William H. Sumner, son of Governor Increase Sumner, the tunnel’s 1934 inauguration marked Boston’s first major underwater roadway, linking East Boston to downtown via a single bored tube.",
    "Modernized in 2016, the Sumner Tunnel now uses cashless tolling, charging $1.50 for Massachusetts E‑Pass holders and $2.05 via Pay‑by‑Plate for non‑E‑Pass vehicles, streamlining traffic into I‑93 northbound."
